00:45:19.120 --> 00:45:21.760
 of a basal arm fracture is that the jagged edges

00:45:21.760 --> 00:45:24.440
 of the broken bone often tear through the dura mater,

00:45:24.440 --> 00:45:25.720
 that protective membrane holding

00:45:25.720 --> 00:45:27.320
 in the cerebrospinal fluid.

00:45:27.320 --> 00:45:30.040
 - We talked about dual tears during lumbar punctures,

00:45:30.040 --> 00:45:32.640
 but here, the fluid isn't leaking into the back.

00:45:32.640 --> 00:45:34.400
 It's leaking out of the face.

00:45:34.400 --> 00:45:36.960
 - The patient will have a clear watery fluid dripping

00:45:36.960 --> 00:45:39.160
 steadily from their nose, rhinorrhea,

00:45:39.160 --> 00:45:42.120
