00:48:43.640 --> 00:48:47.400
 Eye opening, verbal response, and motor response.

00:48:47.400 --> 00:48:49.320
 - The highest score is a 15.

00:48:49.320 --> 00:48:51.560
 You are spontaneously opening your eyes,

00:48:51.560 --> 00:48:54.880
 oriented and conversing, and obeying motor commands.

00:48:54.880 --> 00:48:57.320
 - The lowest possible score is a three.

00:48:57.320 --> 00:48:59.720
 Even a deceased person scores a three.

00:48:59.720 --> 00:49:02.080
 There is no zero on the GCS.

00:49:02.080 --> 00:49:03.600
 - And there is a critical threshold

00:49:03.600 --> 00:49:05.880
 burned into the brain of every medical professional.

00:49:05.880 --> 00:49:08.040
 Less than eight, intubate.

00:49:08.040 --> 00:49:09.520
 - Less than eight, intubate.

00:49:10.400 --> 00:49:12.760
 If your GCS drops to seven or below,

00:49:12.760 --> 00:49:14.880
 you are in a profound coma.

00:49:14.880 --> 00:49:16.720
 - Your brain stem is compromised to the point

00:49:16.720 --> 00:49:19.800
 that you have lost the basic gag and cough reflexes

00:49:19.800 --> 00:49:23.840
 required to protect your own airway from your own saliva.

00:49:23.840 --> 00:49:26.800
 - You must be put on a mechanical ventilator.

00:49:26.800 --> 00:49:29.800
 - The most revealing part of the GCS is the motor response,

00:49:29.800 --> 00:49:32.840
 specifically looking for abnormal posturing.

00:49:32.840 --> 00:49:35.600
 - If you apply a painful stimulus to an unconscious patient,

00:49:35.600 --> 00:49:38.040
 like pressing hard on the nail bed,

00:49:38.040 --> 00:49:40.880
 a healthy brain will try to swat your hand away.

00:49:40.880 --> 00:49:43.440
 - But a damaged brain exhibits stereotype

00:49:43.440 --> 00:49:45.360
