00:54:48.160 --> 00:54:50.800
 - Step seven, the brain also sends signals

00:54:50.800 --> 00:54:53.280
 down the spinal cord, telling all the blood vessels

00:54:53.280 --> 00:54:56.560
 in the body to dilate and relax to relieve the pressure.

00:54:56.560 --> 00:54:57.680
 - But those descending signals

00:54:57.680 --> 00:55:00.200
 hit the exact same roadblock at T6.

00:55:00.200 --> 00:55:01.880
 The relaxation signals cannot reach

00:55:01.880 --> 00:55:03.640
 the lower half of the body.

00:55:03.640 --> 00:55:06.520
 - So look at the absolute chaos happening.

00:55:06.520 --> 00:55:09.560
 You have a body cleanly divided in half at the chest.

00:55:09.560 --> 00:55:12.040
 - Above the T6 injury, the parasympathetic system

00:55:12.040 --> 00:55:13.320
 is in full control.

00:55:13.320 --> 00:55:14.680
 The blood vessels are dilated,

00:55:14.680 --> 00:55:17.480
 causing the patient's face and chest to become bright red,

00:55:17.480 --> 00:55:19.600
 flushed and dripping with sweat.

00:55:19.600 --> 00:55:21.640
 - They have a pounding, terrifying headache

00:55:21.640 --> 00:55:23.160
 from the high blood pressure.

00:55:23.160 --> 00:55:25.120
 Their heart is barely beating.

00:55:25.120 --> 00:55:26.480
 - And below the injury,

00:55:26.480 --> 00:55:29.240
 the rogue sympathetic system is still raging.

00:55:29.240 --> 00:55:31.240
 - The blood vessels are clamped tight.

00:55:31.240 --> 00:55:33.080
 - The skin below the chest is pale,

00:55:33.080 --> 00:55:35.680
 cool to the touch, and completely dry.

00:55:35.680 --> 00:55:38.560
 And the systemic blood pressure remains lethally high

00:55:38.560 --> 00:55:41.040
 because the massive vascular bed of the lower body

00:55:41.040 --> 00:55:42.760
 refuses to open.

00:55:42.760 --> 00:55:44.920
 - A full bladder can cause a fatal stroke

00:55:44.920 --> 00:55:46.200
 in a paralyzed person,

00:55:46.200 --> 00:55:47.960
 all because the communication line is cut

00:55:47.960 --> 00:55:49.640
 and the systems are fighting each other.

00:55:49.640 --> 00:55:51.880
 It is astounding.

00:55:51.880 --> 00:55:53.920
 - So imagine you are the nurse.

00:55:53.920 --> 00:55:56.080
 - Your paraplegic patient suddenly says

00:55:56.080 --> 00:55:57.680
 they have a blinding headache

00:55:57.680 --> 00:55:59.680
